---- MODULE LSH1 ----
\* Two actions generate some steps alike: from 0 to 1 and from 2 to 0 both
\* A and B step. The atom <<A>>_x holds on such a step also where it was
\* generated by B (an A step of the behavior graph, decided by the action
\* that generates a step only together with the other generations of the
\* same step). Every step is an A step except B's 1 -> 0, and a fair
\* behavior cannot repeat that one alone: Prop holds. Deciding <<A>>_x on
\* B's generation of 0 -> 1 as false would admit the cycle 0 -> 1 -> 0
\* without A steps.
EXTENDS Naturals
VARIABLE x
A == x' = (x + 1) % 3
B == x' = IF x = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0
Next == A \/ B
Spec == x = 0 /\ [][Next]_x /\ WF_x(Next)
Prop == []<><<A>>_x
====
